{
 "title": "The Kansas City Massacre",
 "script": [
  "Four lawmen died at a train station, trying to move one prisoner.",
  "Kansas City. Union Station. June 17, 1933.",
  "Federal agents had caught escaped convict Frank Nash the day before.",
  "Now they were walking him to a car, bound for Leavenworth prison.",
  "Then gunmen came at the car and opened fire.",
  "Investigators said they had come to set Nash free.",
  "In about 30 seconds, four lawmen were dead.",
  "Two police officers, a police chief, and a federal agent.",
  "Frank Nash was dead too. The man they came to free.",
  "Within a year, Congress gave federal agents the power to carry guns and make arrests.",
  "Many historians see that morning as the start of the modern FBI."
 ],
